    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Turkic-ruled, Persianised empire that rose from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#oxus">Amu Darya</a> oasis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#khwarazm">Khwarazm</a> to rule from western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#iran">Iran</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#syr-darya">Syr Darya</a>.</li><li>It grew rich on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#silk-road">Silk Road</a> trade, but rapid conquests left it with divided commands and loyalties it never resolved.</li><li>Killing a Mongol envoy in 1218 brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a>'s invasion, which destroyed the empire and opened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#iran">Iran</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#mongols">Mongols</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In 1217 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#ala-ad-din-muhammad-ii">Muhammad II</a> marched on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#baghdad">Baghdad</a> against the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#caliphate">caliph</a>, but the campaign was abandoned when snow overwhelmed his army in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#zagros-mountains">Zagros</a> mountains.</p></aside>
    </section>

